        "setupSummary": "Arthur Pendelton, a veteran school bus driver in Ashtabula, Ohio, notices a shy sixth-grader, Maya Linwood, being cornered by an aggressive eighth-grader, Marcus Vance, while a complaint from Marcus's father threatens Arthur's route.",
        "turnOrMisdirection": "Instead of escalating with authority or defending himself to his supervisor, Arthur deflects Marcus's baiting with a calm, unexpected parable about a crooked fence post, then teaches Maya that a mirror reflects without stepping into the frame.",
        "payoffOrTag": "Transition to the audience by noting that hostile questions are traps designed to pull a speaker into someone else's frame\u2014and that calm curiosity or a well-placed question hands the weight right back.",
